    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41874" root="ورس" body-key="w">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَرِيسٌ</span></b>  A garment <i>dyed with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَرْس</span>; as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَرِسٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَارِسٌ</span></b>  (M) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوَرَّسٌ</span></b> . (M, A.)
You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلْحَفَةٌ وِرِيسَةٌ</span>, (so in some copies of
the S and K) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَرْسِيَّةٌ</span></b> , (as in other copies of
the S and K, and thus in a copy of the Msb,)
[<i>An outer wrapping garment</i>] <i>dyed with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وس</span>;
(S, Msb, K;) <i>i. q.</i> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوَرَّسَةٌ</span></b> ; (K;) which latter
epithet is sometimes used. (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَارِسٌ</span>.

